@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.6.2
@changelog
  - Codename: Look Ma, No ARC!
  - New: RME side-car on the UF1 (macOS). The UF1 remote-controls RME TotalMix FX inside REAPER: hold SHIFT, press MODE, pick RME. Fader, pots and keys move TotalMix; the screens show channel names and colours, levels, EQ, reverb and echo. It is set up in ORC, which it needs: https://github.com/acklin83/ORC
  - New: ORC 1.0.0, the same TotalMix remote on the UF1 without REAPER, as its own free Mac app. When REAPER starts, Rea-Sixty takes the UF1 over from ORC and hands it back when REAPER quits. Settings, Connected devices, Take the UF1 over from ORC (on by default).
  - UF1 pots: after a push the pot ignores turns for 250 ms, so the reset stays (REAPER and side-car)
  - UF1 pot above the fader under FLIP: a push resets what it moves (plug-in default, else 0 dB) instead of centring the pan
  - UF8 send pan: a turn right after the push no longer brings back the old pan
  - UF1 jog with Playhead snap: stops on every grid line, counted from the bar; Shift makes it finer
  - Bindings: a key is Press or Toggle, offered only for actions that can be on or off (replaces Momentary/Toggle/Hold)
